<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Sonny Liston returns two weeks after intake and is seen the same day by Dr. Lindqvist-Owusu. He wore the ambulatory blood pressure monitor for 24 hours last week, including a training session, and had an echocardiogram this morning. His intake blood tests were normal apart from a mildly raised AST and GGT, which were explained to him in plain words as signs that alcohol is affecting his liver. He has cut his drinking from about 25 drinks a week to about 18 by keeping a tally of marks on a card, but found the weekends hard. He feels well and has no headaches, chest pain, breathlessness or palpitations. He wants to know whether he can fight again this year. No thoughts of suicide. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Ambulatory monitoring</td><td>Daytime 146/94, nighttime 132/84, 24-hour 142/91 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Echocardiogram</td><td>Mild concentric LVH (12 mm); ejection fraction 60 percent; normal diastolic function</td></tr><tr><td>Drinking</td><td>About 18 drinks a week, from about 25</td></tr><tr><td>Urine albumin</td><td>18 mg/g, normal</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

